---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import { FOUNDER, CONTACT_EMAIL, REPO_URL, VERSION, contactHref, contactLabel } from '../site';
---
<Base
  title="Company"
  description="RigorRun is built by Erbol Tahirov. Acceptance infrastructure for agents that take real actions — what it is, where it is, and what has not happened yet."
>
  <Section>
    <div class="rr-prose-width">
      <Eyebrow>Company</Eyebrow>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-display font-medium text-balance">
        Agents are being given permission to change things. Almost nothing checks that they did.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-lead text-secondary">
        Software teams have had a way to answer "did this change break the thing that matters" for
        forty years. It is called an acceptance test, and it works because a machine can look at the
        result. Agents arrived without one. The tools that exist score what the model wrote, which is
        the one artefact that cannot tell you whether the work happened.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lead text-secondary">
        RigorRun is the missing half: watch a person do the job once, derive what the rules must be,
        and then verify an agent against the state of the system rather than its own account of
        itself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section ruled tight>
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.3fr] lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-title font-medium">Who</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-support text-secondary">
          RigorRun is built by <span class="text-fg">{FOUNDER}</span>, working on it alone.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-support text-muted">
          There is no company registered behind it yet, no funding, and no employees. Saying so is
          cheaper than being found out, and a product that argues you should check claims rather
          than believe them does not get to make unverifiable ones about itself.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <Button href={contactHref(CONTACT_EMAIL)} variant="secondary">{contactLabel(CONTACT_EMAIL)}</Button>
          <Button href={REPO_URL} variant="secondary" external>GitHub</Button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-title font-medium">Where it actually is</h2>
        <dl class="mt-5 ruled rounded-panel border border-line bg-surface">
          {
            [
              ['Published', `rigorrun@${VERSION} on npm, MIT, with SLSA build provenance`],
              ['Users', 'No external user has run this yet. That is the next thing that matters.'],
              ['Revenue', 'None. There is no price and no billing.'],
              ['Funding', 'None raised.'],
              [
                'Verified against',
                'Four public MCP servers written by somebody else, and a fixture system written for the dogfood test. Not a customer.',
              ],
            ].map(([term, detail]) => (
              <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 px-5 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:gap-6">
                <dt class="w-40 shrink-0 text-micro font-semibold uppercase text-muted">{term}</dt>
                <dd class="text-support text-secondary">{detail}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <p class="mt-5 text-support text-muted">
          If you have an agent doing a job you cannot afford to have silently break, that is the
          conversation worth having. <a class="rr-link" href={contactHref(CONTACT_EMAIL)}>Get in touch.</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
